Cloakroom
=========

The scripts, Compose file, Dockerfile, and examples in this repository are
licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

Cloakroom does not include, modify, or redistribute the CloakBrowser browser.
It builds on the official Docker image `cloakhq/cloakbrowser`, published by
CloakHQ, which Docker downloads directly from Docker Hub on your machine.

- CloakBrowser wrapper code (Python/JS/.NET) is MIT licensed by CloakHQ.
- The CloakBrowser Chromium binary inside that image is proprietary software
  from CloakHQ, governed by its own CloakBrowser Binary License:
  https://github.com/CloakHQ/CloakBrowser/blob/main/BINARY-LICENSE.md

By running Cloakroom you use the CloakBrowser binary and agree to CloakHQ's
Binary License. Cloakroom is an independent community project and is not
affiliated with or endorsed by CloakHQ.

The optional in-browser viewer uses noVNC (MPL-2.0), websockify (LGPL-3.0),
and x11vnc (GPL-2.0), installed from Debian packages at build time.
websockify and x11vnc are unmodified. noVNC is unmodified except that the
build adds one hidden element to its vnc.html (see image/Dockerfile) so
browsers holding a cached older noVNC script still load. noVNC's vnc.html is
BSD-2-Clause per its file header; the rest of noVNC is MPL-2.0.
